## Statement

Let $X$ be a compact finite-dimensional smooth manifold, $K\subseteq X$ a closed smooth submanifold with a chosen collar, $M$ a compact smooth manifold, and $E\to M$ a finite-rank smooth real vector bundle. Let $s:X\times M\to E$ be a continuous family of sections, meaning $s(x,m)\in E_m$ and $(x,m)\mapsto s(x,m)$ is continuous. Assume $x\mapsto s(x,\cdot)$ is continuous in the uniform topology, its restriction to $K$ is continuous in the $C^\infty$ section topology, and for distinct marked points $m_1,\ldots,m_q\in M$ the values $s(x,m_i)=v_i\in E_{m_i}$ are independent of $x$. For every $\varepsilon>0$ there is a family $\widetilde s:X\to\Gamma^\infty(E)$ continuous in the $C^\infty$ topology, equal to $s$ on $K$, equal to $v_i$ at every $m_i$, and satisfying $\sup_{x,m}\|\widetilde s(x,m)-s(x,m)\|<\varepsilon$ for any fixed bundle norm. The straight-line homotopy in each vector fiber from $s$ to $\widetilde s$ fixes $K$ and all marked values.

## Statement references

[Lee, Theorem 6.26, relative Whitney approximation](https://pierre.ag.gerard.web.ulb.be/textbooks/books/Introduction_To_Smooth_Manifolds.pdf)

[Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Chapter 4](https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATch4.pdf)

[May, A Concise Course in Algebraic Topology, Chapter 7](https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf)

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The compact manifolds, vector bundle, collar, family, fixed fiber values and uniform bundle norm of the Statement. Work in ZF + AC to use the supplied smooth partition-of-unity theorem.

[F1] A smooth vector bundle is locally a product with finite-dimensional vector fibers, and its smooth transition functions identify the local section coefficients. [[def-vector-bundle-chart-and-transition-function]]

[F2] On a smooth manifold, a smooth partition of unity subordinate to an open cover supplies smooth cutoff functions supported in the chosen charts. [[def-smooth-partition-of-unity-subordinate-to-an-open-cover]]

[A1] The family on $K$ is continuous into the full $C^\infty$ topology, not merely pointwise smooth in $m$; this is the relative-topology hypothesis used below.

## Proof

1.1 Choose a finite bundle atlas and a subordinate finite smooth partition of unity using compactness and [F1, F2]. In each chart multiply a section coefficient by its partition function, extend by zero within the chart, convolve with a fixed compactly supported smooth mollifier of radius $\delta$, and sum the finitely many resulting local sections. For each $\delta>0$ this defines a linear operator $S_\delta:C^0(M,E)\to\Gamma^\infty(E)$: every output derivative is an integral of the input against a derivative of a fixed smooth kernel, so each $C^r$ seminorm is bounded by a finite constant times the input $C^0$ norm. Uniform continuity of each input on compact chart supports gives $\|S_\delta u-u\|_{C^0}\to0$ for every $u$. Since $x\mapsto s(x,\cdot)$ has compact image in $C^0(M,E)$, a finite subcover argument makes this convergence uniform over $x\in X$. [given, F1, F2, given, construct]

1.2 The family $x\mapsto S_\delta s(x,\cdot)$ is continuous into $C^\infty$ by the seminorm bounds in step 1.1. On a collar $c:K\times[0,2a)\to X$, write $r(c(k,t))=k$ and choose a continuous cutoff $\chi$ equal to $1$ at $t=0$ and supported in $t<a$. Set
$$s_1(x)=S_\delta s(x)+\chi(x)\bigl(s(r(x))-S_\delta s(r(x))\bigr)$$
on the collar and $s_1=S_\delta s$ off it. Every term is a smooth section in $m$ and varies continuously in $C^\infty$ with $x$. At $x\in K$, $s_1(x)=s(x)$. As $x$ approaches $K$, continuity into $C^0$ and the uniform approximation in step 1.1 make the correction uniformly small; choose the collar width and then $\delta$ so $s_1$ remains arbitrarily $C^0$-close to $s$. [given, A1, step 1.1, construct]

2.1 For each marked point choose a bundle chart and a smooth bump $b_i$ supported in that chart with $b_i(m_i)=1$; shrink the charts to be pairwise disjoint. In the chart extend $v_i-s_1(x,m_i)$ as the constant coefficient vector and multiply by $b_i$. The resulting correction $c_i(x,\cdot)$ is a smooth section continuous in $x$ in every $C^r$ seminorm, is zero on $K$ because $s_1=s=v_i$ there, and changes the value at $m_i$ by exactly $v_i-s_1(x,m_i)$. Put $\widetilde s=s_1+\sum_i c_i$. The finite corrections preserve $C^\infty$ continuity and the relative condition. Since the errors at the marked points are bounded by the uniform $C^0$ error from step 1.2 and the bumps have fixed bounded norms, choosing that error sufficiently small gives the prescribed $\varepsilon$ bound. [F1, given, step 1.2, construct]

2.2 For $0\le t\le1$ define $H_t(x,m)=(1-t)s(x,m)+t\widetilde s(x,m)$ in the vector space $E_m$. This is continuous, equals $s$ at $t=0$ and $\widetilde s$ at $t=1$, and is constant on $K$ and at each marked point because both endpoint families agree there. Thus the required relative homotopy exists. [given, step 2.1, algebra] ∎

