        "statement": "Let $X$ be a compact finite-dimensional smooth manifold, $K\\subseteq X$ a closed smooth submanifold with a chosen collar, $M$ a compact smooth manifold, and $E\\to M$ a finite-rank smooth real vector bundle. Let $s:X\\times M\\to E$ be a continuous family of sections, meaning $s(x,m)\\in E_m$ and $(x,m)\\mapsto s(x,m)$ is continuous. Assume $x\\mapsto s(x,\\cdot)$ is continuous in the uniform topology, its restriction to $K$ is continuous in the $C^\\infty$ section topology, and for distinct marked points $m_1,\\ldots,m_q\\in M$ the values $s(x,m_i)=v_i\\in E_{m_i}$ are independent of $x$. For every $\\varepsilon>0$ there is a family $\\widetilde s:X\\to\\Gamma^\\infty(E)$ continuous in the $C^\\infty$ topology, equal to $s$ on $K$, equal to $v_i$ at every $m_i$, and satisfying $\\sup_{x,m}\\|\\widetilde s(x,m)-s(x,m)\\|<\\varepsilon$ for any fixed bundle norm. The straight-line homotopy in each vector fiber from $s$ to $\\widetilde s$ fixes $K$ and all marked values."
