        "statement": "Let $f:S^3\\to S^2$ be a based continuous map. Give $S^2$ an orientation and give the attached $4$-cell its chosen orientation. Its mapping cone is the CW complex $C_f=S^2\\cup_fD^4$, with the basepoint as its $0$-cell. Let $x\\in H^2(C_f;\\mathbb Z)$ be the unique class restricting to the positive generator of $H^2(S^2;\\mathbb Z)$, and let $y\\in H^4(C_f;\\mathbb Z)$ be the generator determined by the oriented $4$-cell. Define the integral mapping-cone Hopf invariant $H(f)\\in\\mathbb Z$ by the equation\n$$x\\smile x=H(f)y.$$"
